# AGENTS.md

Instructions for coding agents (and people) working in this repository.
Created by build-hardening-kit; yours to edit.

## Before you say a change is done

Run the gate. CI runs exactly these commands, so green here means green there.

[% if node %]
- `npm run check` — [[ gate_parts ]]
- `npm test`
[% endif %]
[% if py %]
- `uv run poe check` — [[ gate_parts ]]
- `uv run poe test`
[% endif %]
[% if go %]
- `make check` — [[ gate_parts ]], vet, build
- `make test`
[% endif %]

Fix the cause of a failure. Do not weaken a rule to get green.

## Rules

- Never skip hooks (`--no-verify`) and never disable a check to pass it. CI
  runs every check again, so skipping only moves the failure.
[% if 'lint' in modules and node %]
- Existing lint problems are recorded in `eslint-suppressions.json`. Never add
  to it to hide a new problem. When you fix a recorded one, lower the count with
  `npx eslint --prune-suppressions .`.
[% endif %]
[% if secrets %]
- Never commit a secret (keys, tokens, passwords, connection strings). Read them
  from the environment. The secret scan fails the build on one.
[% endif %]
[% if 'arch-rules' in modules %]
- Database queries live in `dal/` (or `data-access/`, `data_access/`). Call a
  DAL function from application code; never the database client directly.
[% endif %]
- Kit-managed files (`*.hardening.*`[% if ci %], `.github/workflows/hardening.yml`[% endif %]) are
  updated by `uvx copier update --trust`; put your own settings in the entry
  files that import them.
